oolu_01JFr6XCNhJ9n2WDD5MfGhfu", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["compensate_partial", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377470, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JFr6XCNhJ9n2WDD5MfGhfu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381712, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #102 against main, with alex as reviewer. CI passed on the fix branch.\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** on a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #102 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/102). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID. So the fix follows the test and the docstring, not the advisory itself.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J7S69f3FJwsgkDK5fdCD3y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016HzjLbGrCBGEYmgRWBaMRq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014Hgp9QE3ikRZG6YxRphNyx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0148LW9fZfkhXG71tf1UBbU8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RByaTruaScPhQ4ytyg7vFe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Uqosmpr9m1Nyftsm8BMBEQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TUz9dAT1CaBcXrVzkvdfCG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JFr6XCNhJ9n2WDD5MfGhfu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN)", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #102 against main, with alex as reviewer. CI passed on the fix branch.\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, `round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** on a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #102 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/102). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID. So the fix follows the test and the docstring, not the advisory itself.", "type": "text"}]}]}